  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Innovative financial services to support deforestation-free coffee supply chains</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Land development for agriculture is the main cause of deforestation in Uganda. The project contributes to the development of deforestation-free supply chains in coffee production. It promotes agroforestry for the production of shade coffee and other regenerative and climate-friendly agricultural and village practices. It also includes energy efficiency measures and renewable energy solutions at household and farm level. The project combines this with the promotion of blended financing. This includes revolving funds, self-help and savings and internal credit community groups as well as green loans, results-based financing and carbon financing. Local smallholder cooperatives will pool coffee production, jointly market the coffee and sell it directly to small coffee roasters in Germany - applying international standards for sustainable coffee and associated certification systems.</narrative>
  </description>
